###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion:

$\dfrac{\blueE{AE}}{IE}=\dfrac{EI}{EU}$

We picked side $\blueE{\overline{AE}}$ because we need to find its length.

We picked side $\overline{IE}$ because it corresponds to side $\blueE{\overline{AE}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides whose lengths we already knew (or which we could express in terms of $\blue{AE}$).

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle AEI
\\
{\text{long} \atop \text{leg}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{\blueE{AE}}{IE}=\dfrac{EI}{EU}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{hypotenuse}}
\\
&\triangle IEU
\end{array}$
